// Generated from the same campaign authoring source.
    {TEXT("斯卡尔普河的晨雾"),TEXT("Mist over the Scarpe")},
    {TEXT("雪中的前哨"),TEXT("Outposts in the snow")},
{TEXT("雪中的前哨"),TEXT("Outposts in the snow"),TEXT("雪幕后面的枪口")},
{TEXT("雪中的前哨"),TEXT("Outposts in the snow"),TEXT("Guns behind the snow")},
    {TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雪幕中开始。英军最初的推进越过德军前沿，随后遭遇更深的阵地与赶来的预备队；本连争夺其中一段交通壕。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens through snow. British troops cross the first German positions, then meet deeper defences and arriving reserves. This company fights for one approach within that larger battle.")},
    {TEXT("先用步枪占住中央交通壕，再向下一道敌壕推进。把一队留在后方掩护；攻下这两处支点，就能让补充兵通过。"),TEXT("Take the central communication trench, then the first enemy position. Keep a rifle section covering the approach. Securing these two posts opens the route for the following companies.")},
    {TEXT("英军已越过邻段前沿。重新接起中央交通壕，在其后第一处支点挡住追兵；接应从东面失散阵位退下的弟兄。"),TEXT("British troops have crossed the neighbouring front. Reconnect the central trench and first opposing post. Cover the men falling back from the broken positions to the east.")},
    {TEXT("白垩坡上的短交通壕；残雪与雨水弄湿了壕肩。"),TEXT("Short communication trenches cross the chalk slope; snowmelt darkens the parapets.")},
    {TEXT("勒厄的接近线"),TEXT("The approaches to Roeux")},
    {TEXT("化工厂外的前哨"),TEXT("Outposts before the works")},
    {TEXT("勒厄的洞穴与化工厂让阿拉斯东面的推进迟滞。四月十二日的进攻未能拿下村庄，此处命令只涉及外围的接近线。"),TEXT("Caves and the chemical works make Roeux a stubborn obstacle east of Arras. The attack of 12 April does not take the village. The company orders concern its outer approaches only.")},
    {TEXT("投弹班清理近处壕角，步枪班看住开阔地。夺下中央与前沿两处支点；厂房深处仍有机枪，先替下一队清出接近线。"),TEXT("Bombers clear the near trench corners while riflemen cover open ground. Take the central and forward posts. Machine guns remain inside the works; open the approach for the next section.")},
    {TEXT("借破墙保持交叉掩护，不要拥挤在同一壕口。夺回两处外围支点，便能重新给化工厂守军留下交通。"),TEXT("Keep mutually supporting posts among the broken walls. Recover two outer positions to reopen communication with the chemical-works garrison.")},
    {TEXT("厂区外围的破墙与沟渠切断长射界，交通壕旁只有狭窄通路。"),TEXT("Broken boundary walls and drainage cuts interrupt the approaches to the works.")},
    {TEXT("布勒库尔：铁丝的另一面"),TEXT("Bullecourt: beyond the wire")},
    {TEXT("兴登堡线的壕角"),TEXT("Corners of the Hindenburg Line")},
    {TEXT("第二次布勒库尔进攻开始，澳大利亚部队与英国第六十二师攻击兴登堡线。局部壕段被夺取，整个战斗却付出了高昂代价，并未带来战略突破。"),TEXT("The second attack at Bullecourt brings Australian troops and the British 62nd Division against the Hindenburg Line. Some trenches are taken, at severe cost and without a strategic breakthrough.")},
    {TEXT("新配属的枪榴弹组从掩护后抛射 No.23 榴弹，步枪与投弹班利用空当接近。夺住中央与第一道敌壕；让携弹手保有安全通路。"),TEXT("The new rifle-grenade section lobs No.23 bombs from cover. Riflemen and bombers exploit the interval. Secure the central trench and first enemy line; keep a covered route for the carriers.")},
    {TEXT("英澳分队正沿铁丝缺口接近。机枪别追逐单个目标，保持对通路的封锁；在两道相连阵位上恢复防线。"),TEXT("British and Australian sections approach through the wire gaps. Machine guns cover those passages rather than chasing individuals. Restore a connected line through two positions.")},
    {TEXT("密集铁丝沿白垩壕肩展开；弹坑提供接近点，也容易聚集火力。"),TEXT("Dense wire follows chalk parapets. Shell holes offer approaches but attract concentrated fire.")},
    {TEXT("梅西讷的破晓"),TEXT("Dawn at Messines")},
    {TEXT("爆破后的山脊"),TEXT("The ridge after the mines")},
    {TEXT("六月七日，地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军把炮兵、步兵与坦克准备合在一起；幸存守军仍在坑岸与后方阵位抵抗。"),TEXT("On 7 June, mines tear open Messines Ridge. Plumer’s Second Army combines carefully prepared artillery, infantry and tanks. Surviving defenders still resist along crater lips and rear positions.")},
    {TEXT("沿坑岸逐段推进，机枪看住高地通路。完整接起中央与两道纵深壕，让接替部队能够稳固已夺取的山脊。"),TEXT("Advance along the crater lips with machine guns covering the ridge approaches. Connect the central trench and both deeper lines so the relief companies can consolidate the captured ground.")},
    {TEXT("从矿坑边缘重新建立联络。反击夺回本连的交通线，掩护仍在撤出的守军；把还能辨认的壕口接起来，别让伤亡者留在断线后面。"),TEXT("Re-establish communication around the mine craters. Recover the company route and cover the withdrawing survivors. Reconnect the remaining trench mouths before the route is cut again.")},
    {TEXT("陡破坑岸与残存反斜面交错，山脊后的补给湾仍可利用。"),TEXT("Torn crater lips meet surviving reverse slopes; a supply bay remains behind the ridge.")},
    {TEXT("巩固梅西讷山脊"),TEXT("Consolidate the Messines ridge")},
{TEXT("巩固梅西讷山脊"),TEXT("Consolidate the Messines ridge"),TEXT("把山脊接成一条线")},
{TEXT("巩固梅西讷山脊"),TEXT("Consolidate the Messines ridge"),TEXT("Make the ridge a line")},
    {TEXT("山脊反击令"),TEXT("Orders for the ridge counterstroke")},
    {TEXT("梅西讷的战斗没有随第一天结束。德军反击延续数日，英军与澳新部队整顿刚刚夺取的阵地；炮口必须转向新的前沿。"),TEXT("Fighting at Messines continues after the opening day. German counterattacks meet British and Anzac consolidation. Guns and communications must face the newly established front.")},
    {TEXT("中央高地一旦易手，敌军会组织反扑。不要让全部小队向前涌；守住接近线，再夺第一道纵深阵位。"),TEXT("Expect a counterstroke when the central height changes hands. Keep a reserve instead of sending every section forward. Secure the approach, then the first deeper position.")},
    {TEXT("沿仍能相互掩护的壕段反击。英军正在中央支点整备，预备队正沿后方交通壕接近；借烟幕将两处阵位重新接起。"),TEXT("Counterattack through mutually supporting trenches. British troops are consolidating the central post; reserves approach through the rear communication trenches. Reconnect two positions behind smoke.")},
    {TEXT("壕肩尚未完全整修，塌陷处与补给湾把开阔地分成几段。"),TEXT("Unrepaired parapets, collapsed bays and stores divide the open approaches.")},
    {TEXT("雨中的皮尔克姆"),TEXT("Rain at Pilckem")},
    {TEXT("泥地中的据点"),TEXT("Posts in the mud")},
{TEXT("泥地中的据点"),TEXT("Posts in the mud"),TEXT("泥海中的支点")},
{TEXT("泥地中的据点"),TEXT("Posts in the mud"),TEXT("Posts in a sea of mud")},
    {TEXT("第三次伊普尔战役开幕。炮火破坏的排水系统与随后降雨将田野变成积水弹坑；推进必须依靠少数仍然连通的道路和壕道。"),TEXT("Third Ypres opens. Bombardment-damaged drainage and rain turn the fields into waterlogged craters. Movement depends on the few roads and trenches that remain connected.")},
    {TEXT("把机枪放在能掩护通路的位置，烟幕盖住壕间空地。不要同时挤进泥泞的缺口；逐段夺下完整防线。"),TEXT("Place machine guns where they cover the surviving approaches. Smoke the gaps and avoid crowding the mud-bound passages. Capture the connected line one trench at a time.")},
    {TEXT("深泥会拖慢双方，不能代替枪位。守住交通壕，轮换机枪与步枪的掩护；局部反击须等敌军离开烟幕后再判断。"),TEXT("Mud slows both armies but cannot replace a gun position. Preserve the communication trench and alternate rifle and machine-gun cover. Judge counterattacks from visible movement beyond the smoke.")},
    {TEXT("高积水、软泥和较宽的横向战场；铁丝把干燥落脚处分割开。"),TEXT("Waterlogged craters and soft mud spread across a wider front; wire divides the firmer footholds.")},
    {TEXT("朗厄马尔克的混凝土"),TEXT("Concrete at Langemarck")},
    {TEXT("田野里的堡垒"),TEXT("Forts among the fields")},
    {TEXT("八月十六日的进攻继续争夺伊普尔以北高地。分散混凝土据点与泥泞交通让战线难以一并推进；相邻部队的进度并不一致。"),TEXT("The attack of 16 August continues the contest north of Ypres. Scattered concrete positions and muddy communications prevent an even advance. Neighbouring formations gain ground at different rates.")},
    {TEXT("用枪榴弹与壕炮压住第一处据点，再让步枪占壕。只需打通两处相连支点；更远的混凝土堡留给后续部队。"),TEXT("Rifle grenades and mortars suppress the near strongpoint before riflemen occupy it. Open two linked positions. The farther concrete posts belong to the following formations.")},
    {TEXT("不要把混凝土据点当成孤岛。用交通壕维持侧向支援，夺回中央与第一处敌方支点，阻止对手把局部缺口接成通路。"),TEXT("Keep the concrete posts connected. Use communication trenches for lateral support and retake the centre and first opposing post before separate breaches become a route.")},
    {TEXT("狭窄干地绕过深积水，铁丝与掩体形成交错的短射界。"),TEXT("Narrow firm strips skirt deep water; wire and shelter create staggered short fire lanes.")},
    {TEXT("梅宁路：有限推进"),TEXT("Menin Road: a measured advance")},
    {TEXT("梅宁路反击"),TEXT("The Menin Road counterattack")},
{TEXT("梅宁路反击"),TEXT("The Menin Road counterattack"),TEXT("反击走向新的枪口")},
{TEXT("梅宁路反击"),TEXT("The Menin Road counterattack"),TEXT("Counterattacks meet new guns")},
    {TEXT("梅宁路攻势采用有限目标与坚决巩固。普卢默的第二集团军夺取短距离阵地，再用炮火与预备队抵挡德军反击。"),TEXT("At Menin Road, Plumer’s Second Army attacks towards limited objectives and consolidates them. Artillery and reserves then meet German counterattacks against the new positions.")},
    {TEXT("夺下中央与下一道敌壕后即可完成本段任务。敌军会对中央阵位反扑；别越过自己的掩护火线，让预备队接住反击。"),TEXT("Take the centre and the next enemy trench to complete this sector’s limited objective. Expect a counterattack against the centre. Keep reserves within supporting fire.")},
    {TEXT("敌军的新枪位已经转向。不要让反击队单独穿过开阔地；借烟幕压近，在两处阵位恢复连队的联络。"),TEXT("Enemy guns now cover the newly won ground. Do not send counterattacking sections across alone. Close behind smoke and restore company communication through two positions.")},
    {TEXT("较干地表便于展开，但壕角与破损树线仍限制观察。"),TEXT("Firmer ground allows deployment, while trench corners and shattered tree lines restrict observation.")},
    {TEXT("康布雷的缺口"),TEXT("The gap at Cambrai")},
    {TEXT("康布雷：夺回交通线"),TEXT("Cambrai: reopen the route")},
    {TEXT("康布雷展示了集中坦克、突然炮击与步兵协同的威力。十一月三十日，德军反击夺回大片失地；任何连队的局部成功都没有结束整场战役。"),TEXT("Cambrai demonstrates massed tanks, surprise artillery and infantry cooperation. On 30 November, German counterattacks recover much lost ground. A company’s local success does not decide the whole battle.")},
    {TEXT("Mark IV 已列入配属。让步枪跟住坦克清理壕口，机枪掩护缺口侧翼；夺下全线后仍要防备反扑。"),TEXT("Mark IV tanks join the attachment list. Riflemen follow to clear trench mouths while machine guns cover the breach’s flank. Secure the entire company line.")},
    {TEXT("三十日晨，反击命令已到。先接通中央交通，再逐壕展开；缴获坦克仍在后方整修，步枪与机枪组先把道路打开。"),TEXT("On the morning of the thirtieth, the counterattack order arrives. Reconnect the centre, then work through the trenches. Captured tanks remain under repair; rifles and machine guns must open the road.")},
    {TEXT("坚实田地、长射界与密集兴登堡线铁丝并存。"),TEXT("Firm fields and long sight lines meet dense Hindenburg-Line wire.")},
    {TEXT("布尔隆：留住出口"),TEXT("Bourlon: keep the exit")},
    {TEXT("布尔隆的撤退通路"),TEXT("Withdrawal routes at Bourlon")},
{TEXT("布尔隆的撤退通路"),TEXT("Withdrawal routes at Bourlon"),TEXT("突出部的咽喉")},
{TEXT("布尔隆的撤退通路"),TEXT("Withdrawal routes at Bourlon"),TEXT("The salient’s throat")},
    {TEXT("康布雷突出部在反击中遭到挤压。布尔隆一带的林缘与交通线成为关键；英军随后撤离部分突出部，战线再次收拢。"),TEXT("Counterattacks compress the Cambrai salient. The Bourlon approaches and communications become crucial. British troops subsequently withdraw from part of the salient, narrowing the front again.")},
    {TEXT("夺回中央与第一处敌壕，掩护林缘友军撤出。把机枪留在出口旁，待后队通过再轮换；不能让撤出的连队在开阔地失去掩护。"),TEXT("Recover the centre and first opposing trench to cover troops leaving the woodland edge. Keep machine guns by the exit until the following men pass. Do not abandon them in the open.")},
    {TEXT("压住林缘出口，同时让后队保持掩护。敌军会为交通线反扑；拿下两道相连支点，比无掩护地追逐撤退者更重要。"),TEXT("Cover the woodland exit without losing support from the rear. Expect a counterstroke for the communication route. Two linked posts matter more than an unsupported pursuit.")},
    {TEXT("被炮火打断的林缘、洼地与狭窄出口使预备队格外重要。"),TEXT("Shell-broken woodland edges and narrow exits make a reserve essential.")},
    {TEXT("冬夜巡逻簿"),TEXT("The winter patrol book")},
    {TEXT("铁丝前的脚印"),TEXT("Footprints before the wire")},
    {TEXT("冬季的康布雷前线仍在巡逻、抓俘和修壕。雨雪留下新的脚印，前哨等待对面的接防消息。"),TEXT("Winter patrols, prisoner raids and trench repairs continue on the Cambrai front. Sleet leaves fresh tracks as outposts await word of the enemy relief."),TEXT("大攻势之间，巡逻、抓俘与修壕没有停止。本关是康布雷战区冬季活动的连级合成情景，不代表一场虚构的正式大会战。")},
    {TEXT("接通中央与敌方前哨。为保持行动隐蔽，本次不配属坦克、野炮与空中任务；用步枪、投弹班和烟幕完成短促出击。"),TEXT("Secure the centre and enemy outpost. Tanks, field artillery and air missions are not attached to this small raid. Riflemen, bombers and smoke must carry the short action.")},
    {TEXT("巡逻发现对方前哨活动。夺回中央与近处支点，重建观察；此次没有坦克、野炮和机队接令，依靠能互相掩护的分队。"),TEXT("Patrols report activity at the opposing outpost. Restore observation through the centre and near post. No tanks, field artillery or aircraft answer this raid’s orders.")},
    {TEXT("湿冷低光照与稀疏积水；交通壕近，携行装备限制明确。"),TEXT("Cold, wet ground and low light favour a compact action with restricted attachments.")},
    {TEXT("雾里的后卫"),TEXT("Rearguard in the mist")},
    {TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势"),TEXT("Operation Michael")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势"),TEXT("Operation Michael"),TEXT("米夏埃尔：穿过薄弱处")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势"),TEXT("Operation Michael"),TEXT("Michael: through the weak points")},
    {TEXT("三月二十一日，德军米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮击中展开。英军第五集团军后撤，德军前进很快，却无法始终保持补给与邻军联络。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens on 21 March through fog and concentrated bombardment. British Fifth Army retreats. German advances outpace parts of their supply and lateral communications.")},
    {TEXT("夺回中央与下一处支点，打通被截断的后撤路线。机枪掩护，烟幕遮住轮换；第五集团军仍在后撤，先把断线两侧的人接起来。"),TEXT("Retake the centre and next post to reconnect the withdrawal route. Machine guns cover relief behind smoke. Fifth Army is still falling back; link the men on either side of the breach.")},
    {TEXT("A7V 开始列入本连配属。别让装甲独自越过步兵，抢回中继补给湾再展开纵深进攻；储备抵达后才能保持推进。"),TEXT("A7V tanks become available to the company. Keep infantry with the armour. Reopen the forward supply bay before pushing deeper so ammunition can follow.")},
    {TEXT("浓雾削短观察距离，旧壕与补给湾仍能维持前后联络。"),TEXT("Fog shortens observation; old trenches and supply bays still connect front and rear.")},
    {TEXT("利斯河：恢复侧翼联络"),TEXT("The Lys: restore flank contact")},
{TEXT("利斯河：恢复侧翼联络"),TEXT("The Lys: restore flank contact"),TEXT("利斯河：接上侧翼")},
{TEXT("利斯河：恢复侧翼联络"),TEXT("The Lys: restore flank contact"),TEXT("The Lys: reconnect the flank")},
    {TEXT("乔治特的通路"),TEXT("The approaches of Georgette")},
    {TEXT("四月九日，德军在利斯河方向发动攻势，葡萄牙与英军正面承受冲击。道路、河沟和相邻部队的接合部决定了局部防线能否重新组织。"),TEXT("On 9 April, the German offensive on the Lys strikes Portuguese and British positions. Roads, drainage cuts and formation boundaries determine whether local defences can reconnect.")},
    {TEXT("侧翼联络已中断。夺回中央交通壕与第一处支点，烟幕盖住道路交叉口；葡萄牙邻段的遭遇提醒你，孤立的枪位守不住整条线。"),TEXT("The flank connection is broken. Retake the centre and first post, smoking the road junction. The pressure on the Portuguese neighbour shows why isolated gun positions cannot hold a line.")},
    {TEXT("沿道路缺口接近，观察烟幕后是否还有枪位。先夺两处相连支点，让后续部队通过；推进不能让携弹队掉在河沟后面。"),TEXT("Approach through the road gaps and watch for guns beyond smoke. Take two connected posts for the following troops. Keep carriers from falling behind the drainage cuts.")},
    {TEXT("平缓低地、河沟与宽泥带把可通行地面分开。"),TEXT("Low fields, drainage cuts and broad wet strips divide the usable ground.")},
    {TEXT("维莱布勒托讷：装甲交锋"),TEXT("Villers-Bretonneux: tank combat")},
{TEXT("维莱布勒托讷：装甲交锋"),TEXT("Villers-Bretonneux: tank combat"),TEXT("维莱布勒托讷：钢铁相遇")},
{TEXT("维莱布勒托讷：装甲交锋"),TEXT("Villers-Bretonneux: tank combat"),TEXT("Villers-Bretonneux: armour meets armour")},
    {TEXT("通向亚眠的村口"),TEXT("The village approach to Amiens")},
    {TEXT("四月二十四日，维莱布勒托讷出现坦克之间的交战。德军攻入村庄，澳大利亚与英国部队随后反击；次日村庄被夺回。"),TEXT("On 24 April, tanks fight tanks at Villers-Bretonneux. German forces enter the village; Australian and British counterattacks follow, retaking it the next day.")},
    {TEXT("从村外接近线反击。让反装甲炮观察到敌车，步枪掩护自己的坦克；接起中央与两道纵深壕，恢复村口通路。"),TEXT("Counterattack through the village approaches. Give the anti-tank gun a view of enemy armour while riflemen accompany your tanks. Reconnect the centre and both deeper trenches.")},
    {TEXT("村口的进攻命令已经送到。步枪护住坦克侧面，机枪看住道路交叉；夺下通路后立即整备，村外的敌军还会回来。"),TEXT("Orders for the village approach have arrived. Riflemen cover the tanks and machine guns watch the junctions. Secure the route and prepare immediately; enemy troops outside the village will return.")},
    {TEXT("破墙、果园残株与道路交叉形成装甲的观察窗口。"),TEXT("Broken walls, orchard remains and junctions create intermittent views for armour.")},
    {TEXT("亚眠的低云"),TEXT("Low cloud over Amiens")},
    {TEXT("八月八日的断线"),TEXT("Broken lines on 8 August")},
    {TEXT("亚眠攻势把炮兵、坦克、步兵与航空力量结合起来。澳大利亚和加拿大部队向东推进，法军在南侧作战；德军遭遇严重挫折，百日攻势由此展开。"),TEXT("Amiens combines artillery, tanks, infantry and aircraft. Australian and Canadian formations advance with the French to the south. Germany suffers a severe reverse as the Hundred Days begin.")},
    {TEXT("Whippet 可随较快的跟进部队行动。榴霰弹截断暴露的援兵，步枪守住装甲留下的壕口。"),TEXT("Whippets become available for the following movement. Shrapnel catches exposed reinforcements. Riflemen secure the trench mouths left behind the armour.")},
    {TEXT("Tankgewehr 组与整修的缴获坦克归队。重枪架稳后再开火，携弹手守住侧面；夺回中央与第一处支点，把撤出的部队接回交通壕。"),TEXT("Tankgewehr teams and repaired captured tanks join the company. Support the heavy rifle before firing and keep its carrier beside it. Recover the centre and first post to bring withdrawing troops into the communication trench.")},
    {TEXT("较宽田野和残存村界适合装甲展开，薄雾仍会干扰观察。"),TEXT("Broad fields and surviving village boundaries allow armour to deploy through intermittent mist.")},
    {TEXT("越过白垩田野"),TEXT("Across the chalk fields")},
    {TEXT("斯卡尔普的后卫"),TEXT("Rearguards on the Scarpe")},
    {TEXT("百日攻势继续越过旧阵地。加拿大军在斯卡尔普方向推进，德军依托白垩壕、铁丝和村落掩护后撤。"),TEXT("The Hundred Days carry the advance across old positions. The Canadian Corps pushes along the Scarpe while German rearguards use chalk trenches, wire and villages.")},
    {TEXT("工兵随队开路，枪榴弹组压住近壕。编制超出岗位后，先在作战室挑选配属；让炮火、观察和清障各有位置。"),TEXT("Pioneers open the route while rifle grenades suppress near trenches. Choose the attachments before departure: observation, artillery and clearance each need a place in the company order.")},
    {TEXT("工兵与 Wex 分队已经赶到。夺回中央与近处支点，给后卫留下交通；再以烟幕掩护轮换，沉重装备旁要有人照应。"),TEXT("Pioneers and Wex sections have arrived. Recover the centre and near post to preserve the rearguard route. Cover relief with smoke and keep companions beside the heavy equipment.")},
    {TEXT("白垩断面、残线铁丝与可疑弹药沿田界聚集。"),TEXT("Chalk cuts, old wire and suspect ammunition cluster along field boundaries.")},
    {TEXT("里克瓦尔的明渠"),TEXT("The open cut at Riqueval")},
    {TEXT("守住运河土坡"),TEXT("Hold the canal banks")},
    {TEXT("九月二十九日，英军第四十六师在里克瓦尔附近突击圣康坦运河明渠，夺下未被炸毁的桥。北面的贝利库尔隧道上方，澳大利亚与配属美军同时攻向兴登堡防线。本连负责明渠边的一段接近线；破损土坡、纤道和少数通路决定谁能渡越。"),TEXT("On 29 September, the British 46th Division assaults the open St Quentin Canal cutting near Riqueval and secures a bridge before it can be destroyed. To the north, Australian and attached American troops attack above the Bellicourt tunnel. This company fights for one approach to the exposed cut, where battered banks and towpaths determine the crossing.")},
    {TEXT("工兵先打开明渠两侧的障碍，法军 Schilt 分遣队在烟幕后清理近处掩体。抓住破损坡岸留下的通路；渡口烟幕影响双方观察，炮击前确认自己人的位置。"),TEXT("Pioneers open the obstacles along the cut. The attached French Schilt section clears near shelters behind smoke. Use the damaged bank approaches; crossing smoke blinds both sides, so check friendly positions before ordering fire.")},
    {TEXT("错开的枪位压住两侧坡岸，工兵照看纤道。中央一旦失守，预备队沿未坍塌的通路反击；接起中央与近处阵位，掩护下一批守军撤离明渠。"),TEXT("Staggered guns cover both banks while pioneers maintain the towpath. If the centre falls, reserves counterattack through an intact approach. Reconnect the centre and near post to cover the next men withdrawing from the open cut.")},
    {TEXT("下挖的明渠、两侧破损土坡和残存纤道贯穿战场；两处降坡通路可供部队渡越。"),TEXT("An open excavated canal, damaged opposing banks and a surviving towpath cross the field; two graded breaches permit passage.")},
    {TEXT("铁路切口"),TEXT("The railway cutting")},
{TEXT("铁路切口"),TEXT("The railway cutting"),TEXT("切口里的钢铁")},
{TEXT("铁路切口"),TEXT("The railway cutting"),TEXT("Steel in the railway cutting")},
    {TEXT("塞勒河：争夺铁路"),TEXT("The Selle: contest the railway")},
{TEXT("塞勒河：争夺铁路"),TEXT("The Selle: contest the railway"),TEXT("塞勒河：留住铁轨")},
{TEXT("塞勒河：争夺铁路"),TEXT("The Selle: contest the railway"),TEXT("The Selle: keep the railway")},
    {TEXT("追击抵达塞勒河谷，铁路切口成为后卫据点。本连须打通路堤旁的接近线，为后续部队开路。"),TEXT("The pursuit reaches the Selle valley, where a railway cutting forms a rearguard post. The company must open the embankment approaches for the following troops."),TEXT("塞勒河战役把追击带进河谷与铁路切口。本关的装甲列车是以战时铁路火力为基础的合成局部情景，并非声称某列具名车辆在此参战。")},
    {TEXT("敌方列车沿切口活动。反装甲火力盯住炮车，工兵检查接近线；夺下中央与下一处支点，切断它对本段的观察。"),TEXT("The enemy train works the cutting. Anti-armour fire covers the gun car while pioneers inspect the approach. Take the centre and next post to deny its observation of this sector.")},
    {TEXT("铁路支援只能沿轨道机动。守住附近步兵联络，让列车掩护轮换；接起两道支点，为撤运保住通路。"),TEXT("Railway support can move only along the track. Keep infantry communication beside it while the train covers relief. Reconnect two positions to preserve the evacuation route.")},
    {TEXT("湿润河谷与路堤并列；轨旁障碍有明确通路，不可横穿车体。"),TEXT("A wet valley follows the embankment; obstacles leave defined approaches beside the train.")},
    {TEXT("瓦朗谢讷的门外"),TEXT("Before Valenciennes")},
    {TEXT("城外最后的枪位"),TEXT("The last guns outside town")},
    {TEXT("加拿大军在十一月初攻取瓦朗谢讷，推进越来越接近仍有居民的城镇。守军后撤，炮火计划必须考虑没有离开的平民。"),TEXT("The Canadian Corps takes Valenciennes in early November. The advance reaches towns that still hold civilians. German rearguards withdraw while fire plans must account for those who remain.")},
    {TEXT("只夺城外中央与第一处阵位，不把整个居民区当作目标。毒气与空中轰炸不列入命令，保留工兵和可观察的地面火力。"),TEXT("Secure the centre and first post outside town. The inhabited district is not a blanket target. Gas and aerial bombing are excluded; retain pioneers and observed ground support.")},
    {TEXT("控制城外通路，掩护后卫离开。毒气与空中轰炸均未获批准；用相互支援的枪位完成两处阵位的局部反击。"),TEXT("Control the outer route to cover departing rearguards. Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised. Mutually supporting guns must recover the two local positions.")},
    {TEXT("城边破墙、果园与浅沟形成短射界，火力选择受到限制。"),TEXT("Boundary walls, orchards and shallow cuts create short fire lanes under restricted support orders.")},
    {TEXT("停战以前的清晨"),TEXT("Morning before the armistice")},
    {TEXT("带回还能归队的人"),TEXT("Bring back those who can return")},
    {TEXT("桑布尔攻势与勒凯努瓦的作战在十一月四日展开。新西兰部队越过城墙；西线尚未停火，最后一周的每一条通路仍有人为之伤亡。"),TEXT("The Sambre offensive and the action at Le Quesnoy open on 4 November. New Zealand troops cross the walls. The Western Front has not yet ceased fire, and its final approaches still cost lives.")},
    {TEXT("把连队练成的分工带到最后一段通路。工兵先行，步枪占壕，装甲与炮火只打能够确认的目标；让接替部队沿完整交通线通过。"),TEXT("Bring the company’s hard-learned cooperation to the final approach. Pioneers lead, rifles occupy, armour and artillery engage observed targets. Open the complete route for the following troops.")},
    {TEXT("停战电报尚未抵达。先把中央与近处支点重新接起，机枪留在出口掩护；把还能归队的人带回来，再让后卫轮换。"),TEXT("The armistice order has not arrived. Reconnect the centre and near post, keeping machine guns at the exit. Bring back the men who can still return, then relieve the rearguard.")},
    {TEXT("居民区边缘的壕道通向运河，残余障碍仍需工兵检查。"),TEXT("Trenches along inhabited edges lead towards the canal; pioneers must still inspect surviving obstacles.")},
// V50 company dispatches
{TEXT("出发行军表"),TEXT("Marching orders")},
{TEXT("出发行军表"),TEXT("Marching orders"),TEXT("第一张行军表")},
{TEXT("出发行军表"),TEXT("Marching orders"),TEXT("The First March Table")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯城后的地道挤满待命士兵。炮兵将最后一份测地表送进连部，军士核对各班的出发位置与目标。"),TEXT("The tunnels behind Arras fill with waiting troops. A final survey table reaches company headquarters as NCOs check each section's starting position and objective.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯城后的地道挤满待命士兵。炮兵将最后一份测地表送进连部，军士核对各班的出发位置与目标。"),TEXT("The tunnels behind Arras fill with waiting troops. A final survey table reaches company headquarters as NCOs check each section's starting position and objective."),TEXT("阿拉斯城后的地道挤满出发的人。炮兵把最后一份测地表送进连部，士官逐一核对各班的去向；从今天起，战报上的每一条线都要有人亲自走过。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯城后的地道挤满待命士兵。炮兵将最后一份测地表送进连部，军士核对各班的出发位置与目标。"),TEXT("The tunnels behind Arras fill with waiting troops. A final survey table reaches company headquarters as NCOs check each section's starting position and objective."),TEXT("The tunnels behind Arras fill with men waiting to move. A final survey table reaches the company office. NCOs check where each section must go. From today, every line on the report will have to be crossed on foot.")},
{TEXT("连部电话簿"),TEXT("The Company Telephone Book")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前沿的几处枪位失去电话联络。连部重新标出枪位与备用路口，联络兵接替被炮火切断的电话线。"),TEXT("Several gun posts on the Arras front lose telephone contact. Headquarters updates the list of posts and reserve junctions, with runners carrying messages where shellfire has cut the wire.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前沿的几处枪位失去电话联络。连部重新标出枪位与备用路口，联络兵接替被炮火切断的电话线。"),TEXT("Several gun posts on the Arras front lose telephone contact. Headquarters updates the list of posts and reserve junctions, with runners carrying messages where shellfire has cut the wire."),TEXT("阿拉斯前沿的电话簿少了几个回答。连部把各枪位与备用路口重新编在一页上；炮火能割断铜线，却不能让每一个联络兵同时停下。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前沿的几处枪位失去电话联络。连部重新标出枪位与备用路口，联络兵接替被炮火切断的电话线。"),TEXT("Several gun posts on the Arras front lose telephone contact. Headquarters updates the list of posts and reserve junctions, with runners carrying messages where shellfire has cut the wire."),TEXT("Several entries in the Arras telephone book no longer answer. The company rewrites its gun positions and reserve junctions on one sheet. Shellfire may cut the wire, but it cannot stop every runner at once.")},
{TEXT("连部获得一枚研究点。既有装备可以立即安排一次基础研习。"),TEXT("The company gains one research point for an immediate basic improvement.")},
{TEXT("坑岸上的测地桩"),TEXT("Survey Stakes on the Crater Rim")},
{TEXT("梅西讷攻击前，第二集团军复核测绘、爆破点与炮兵表。澳新邻段送来的草图补全了接合部坐标。"),TEXT("Before Messines, Second Army checks its surveys, mine positions and fire tables. Sketches from the neighbouring ANZAC sector complete the junction coordinates."),TEXT("梅西讷攻势前，第二集团军把测绘、地下爆破与炮兵表反复核对。澳新邻段送来接合处的草图；图纸不会替步兵占壕，却让第一批炮弹少走一段传令路。")},
{TEXT("备用线还在"),TEXT("The Spare Line Still Answers")},
{TEXT("山脊上的电话被爆破震断，反斜面的备用接线箱却还通着。联络兵从坑岸找回炮兵观察员，把幸存支点逐个报给后方。"),TEXT("The explosions cut the ridge telephone, but a spare junction box on the reverse slope still answers. Runners recover an artillery observer from the crater rim and report the surviving posts to the batteries.")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。梅西讷两次行动的首轮野炮提前二十二秒，首轮烟幕后再整备缩短八秒。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. In both Messines operations, the first field barrage prepares 22 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm takes eight seconds less.")},
{TEXT("木板路上的弹药"),TEXT("Ammunition on the Duckboards")},
{TEXT("佛兰德排水系统被炮火打碎后，雨水没有地方可去。重炮弹在后方卸下，能由人背负的壕炮弹先被送往前沿；军需官把这项安排写进了下一次行动的清单。"),TEXT("With the Flanders drainage shattered, the rain has nowhere to go. Heavy shells are unloaded farther back. Mortar rounds that men can carry go forward first, and the quartermaster extends the arrangement to the next operation.")},
{TEXT("肩上的最后一箱"),TEXT("The Last Crate on Their Shoulders")},
{TEXT("炮车陷进泥地，壕炮弹改由携弹队背送。重炮仍在后方等待通路，前沿先用已经抵达的弹药。"),TEXT("Gun wagons sink into the mud. Bearers shoulder mortar bombs while heavy batteries wait for a route forward. The front uses the ammunition already through."),TEXT("炮车陷在泥里，携弹手把壕炮弹分装到肩上。后方仍有炮，却不是每一种炮都能按时接上前沿；这两次行动必须先依靠搬得过去的火力。")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。皮尔克姆与朗厄马尔克的迫击炮提前十八秒，首轮野炮延后二十四秒。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. At Pilckem and Langemarck, mortars prepare 18 seconds earlier; the first field barrage takes 24 seconds longer to prepare.")},
{TEXT("先拿下，再站稳"),TEXT("Take It, Then Hold It")},
{TEXT("梅宁路的进攻集中炮火，逐段夺取有限目标。步兵占领后立即巩固阵地，预备队准备迎击德军反攻。"),TEXT("The Menin Road attack concentrates artillery on limited objectives. Infantry consolidate each gain while reserves prepare for German counterattacks.")},
{TEXT("梅宁路的进攻集中炮火，逐段夺取有限目标。步兵占领后立即巩固阵地，预备队准备迎击德军反攻。"),TEXT("The Menin Road attack concentrates artillery on limited objectives. Infantry consolidate each gain while reserves prepare for German counterattacks."),TEXT("梅宁路的进攻把炮兵计划压在有限的地段上，预备队等着对付德军反击。少走的几百码并不轻松；只是命令终于为占领之后发生的事留下了位置。")},
{TEXT("梅宁路的进攻集中炮火，逐段夺取有限目标。步兵占领后立即巩固阵地，预备队准备迎击德军反攻。"),TEXT("The Menin Road attack concentrates artillery on limited objectives. Infantry consolidate each gain while reserves prepare for German counterattacks."),TEXT("At the Menin Road, artillery plans concentrate on limited ground and reserves wait for the German counterattacks. A few hundred fewer yards are no easier; the orders finally make room for what follows the capture.")},
{TEXT("反击队集合处"),TEXT("The Counterattack Assembly Point")},
{TEXT("英军正把新占的地段筑成枪线。炮兵观察员与反击队改在同一处路口交换消息，毒气弹也已送到；若失去联络，这些火力同样会封住自己的路。"),TEXT("The British turn each new gain into a gun line. Observers and counterattack parties now exchange reports at the same junction. Gas shells have arrived, but without liaison their fire can close German roads as easily as British ones.")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。毒气支援开放；防毒面具须另行研发。中央易手会触发反击。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. Gas support is available; respirators require separate research. Taking the centre draws a counterattack.")},
{TEXT("履带与时刻表"),TEXT("Tracks and Timetables")},
{TEXT("康布雷的坚实地面给了坦克一次难得的机会。炮兵使用预先计算的射击数据，步兵与履带按时出发；最初的突破之后，补给与接替仍要沿原路跟上。"),TEXT("The firm ground at Cambrai gives tanks an unusual opportunity. Guns use predicted fire and the infantry move to the same timetable as the tracks. Beyond the first success, supplies and relief must still follow the original road.")},
{TEXT("康布雷反击令"),TEXT("Orders for the Cambrai Counterattack")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，德军反击康布雷突出部，重新争夺道路。直射炮迎击坦克，机枪掩护步兵接替；缴获车辆仍在工场修复。"),TEXT("On 30 November, German troops counterattack the Cambrai salient and contest its roads. Direct-fire guns engage tanks, machine guns cover infantry reliefs, and captured vehicles remain in the repair workshops.")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，德军反击康布雷突出部，重新争夺道路。直射炮迎击坦克，机枪掩护步兵接替；缴获车辆仍在工场修复。"),TEXT("On 30 November, German troops counterattack the Cambrai salient and contest its roads. Direct-fire guns engage tanks, machine guns cover infantry reliefs, and captured vehicles remain in the repair workshops."),TEXT("英军突出部已经形成，十一月三十日的反击重新争夺那些道路。直射炮盯住坦克，机枪替步兵接续掩护；缴获车辆要等修复，不会因为战报漂亮就立刻归队。")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，德军反击康布雷突出部，重新争夺道路。直射炮迎击坦克，机枪掩护步兵接替；缴获车辆仍在工场修复。"),TEXT("On 30 November, German troops counterattack the Cambrai salient and contest its roads. Direct-fire guns engage tanks, machine guns cover infantry reliefs, and captured vehicles remain in the repair workshops."),TEXT("The British salient has formed. On 30 November the counterattack contests its roads again. Direct-fire guns watch the tanks and machine guns cover the infantry relief. Captured vehicles must wait for repairs, whatever the reports claim.")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。康布雷与布尔隆首轮野炮提前二十八秒，迫击炮提前五秒。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. At Cambrai and Bourlon, the first field barrage prepares 28 seconds earlier and mortars five seconds earlier.")},
{TEXT("轻装巡逻"),TEXT("Light patrol")},
{TEXT("轻装巡逻"),TEXT("Light patrol"),TEXT("只带能背走的东西")},
{TEXT("轻装巡逻"),TEXT("Light patrol"),TEXT("Only What Can Be Carried")},
{TEXT("冬季没有大会战，却没有平静的前线。抓俘、巡逻和修壕照常进行；这一夜的炮兵联络被划去，轻装分队带回的消息将决定春季的部署。"),TEXT("Winter brings no great offensive, but the front is not quiet. Prisoner raids, patrols and trench work continue. Tonight the battery liaison is struck out; the reports carried back by light sections will shape the spring dispositions.")},
{TEXT("铁丝前的脚印"),TEXT("Tracks Before the Wire")},
{TEXT("春季攻势尚在准备，前哨先查探敌军换防。巡逻队携烟弹沿低地接近，今晚没有重炮支援。"),TEXT("As preparations for the spring offensive continue, outposts investigate enemy reliefs. Patrols approach through low ground with smoke bombs and no heavy artillery support tonight.")},
{TEXT("春季攻势尚在准备，前哨先查探敌军换防。巡逻队携烟弹沿低地接近，今晚没有重炮支援。"),TEXT("As preparations for the spring offensive continue, outposts investigate enemy reliefs. Patrols approach through low ground with smoke bombs and no heavy artillery support tonight."),TEXT("春季攻势尚在准备，前沿先要弄清对面换来了谁。巡逻携带的烟弹比口粮还仔细地包好；重炮一开火，今晚的任务就变成了另一回事。")},
{TEXT("春季攻势尚在准备，前哨先查探敌军换防。巡逻队携烟弹沿低地接近，今晚没有重炮支援。"),TEXT("As preparations for the spring offensive continue, outposts investigate enemy reliefs. Patrols approach through low ground with smoke bombs and no heavy artillery support tonight."),TEXT("The spring offensive is still being prepared. First the outposts must discover who now holds the opposite line. Patrols wrap their smoke bombs as carefully as their rations. Heavy gunfire would turn tonight into a different operation.")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。本次只配属轻装部队与烟幕；装甲、野炮、壕炮及机队停止接令。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. Only light troops and smoke are attached: armour, field guns, mortars and aircraft stand down for this operation.")},
{TEXT("西去的传令兵"),TEXT("Runners Heading West")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势迫使英军第五集团军后撤。法军向受威胁的接合部靠拢，连部收到新的联络表和补充兵，准备接应失散部队。"),TEXT("Operation Michael forces British Fifth Army back. French troops move towards the threatened junction as a new liaison list and replacements reach the company, ready to receive scattered units.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势迫使英军第五集团军后撤。法军向受威胁的接合部靠拢，连部收到新的联络表和补充兵，准备接应失散部队。"),TEXT("Operation Michael forces British Fifth Army back. French troops move towards the threatened junction as a new liaison list and replacements reach the company, ready to receive scattered units."),TEXT("英军第五集团军的防线在米夏埃尔攻势下后撤。法军向受威胁的接合部靠拢，连部收到一份新的联络表和一批补充兵；路还在，人就还有地方集合。")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势迫使英军第五集团军后撤。法军向受威胁的接合部靠拢，连部收到新的联络表和补充兵，准备接应失散部队。"),TEXT("Operation Michael forces British Fifth Army back. French troops move towards the threatened junction as a new liaison list and replacements reach the company, ready to receive scattered units."),TEXT("Fifth Army falls back under Operation Michael. French troops move towards the threatened junction, and the company receives a new liaison list with a draft of replacements. While a road remains, scattered men still have somewhere to gather.")},
{TEXT("从东线来的列车"),TEXT("Trains from the East")},
{TEXT("东线部队陆续运到西线。突击操练与弹药分配令送到连部，携弹队准备跟随攻势前移。"),TEXT("Troops from the Eastern Front arrive in the west. Assault drills and ammunition orders reach the companies as carrying parties prepare to follow the advance."),TEXT("俄国退出战争后，德国把更多兵力转向西线。连队收到的不是一场已经赢下的战争，而是突击操练、弹药与出发时刻；纵深越大，补给线也会越长。")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。米夏埃尔与利斯河行动开场士气增加六，首轮野炮提前二十秒，首轮烟幕后再整备缩短十二秒。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. Michael and the Lys begin with six additional morale; their first field barrage prepares 20 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm takes 12 seconds less.")},
{TEXT("同一张炮兵表"),TEXT("One Artillery Table")},
{TEXT("亚眠攻势中，澳大利亚、加拿大、英国和法国部队在相邻地段推进。炮兵、坦克与飞机支援步兵，携弹队跟进补给，信号员维持各部队联络。"),TEXT("At Amiens, Australian, Canadian, British and French formations advance in neighbouring sectors. Guns, tanks and aircraft support the infantry, ammunition parties bring supplies forward, and signallers maintain contact between units.")},
{TEXT("亚眠攻势中，澳大利亚、加拿大、英国和法国部队在相邻地段推进。炮兵、坦克与飞机支援步兵，携弹队跟进补给，信号员维持各部队联络。"),TEXT("At Amiens, Australian, Canadian, British and French formations advance in neighbouring sectors. Guns, tanks and aircraft support the infantry, ammunition parties bring supplies forward, and signallers maintain contact between units."),TEXT("亚眠的进攻把澳大利亚、加拿大、英国和法国部队置于相邻战线上。炮兵、坦克与飞机共同为步兵打开通路；携弹队和信号员的工作，决定这张表能不能一直走下去。")},
{TEXT("亚眠攻势中，澳大利亚、加拿大、英国和法国部队在相邻地段推进。炮兵、坦克与飞机支援步兵，携弹队跟进补给，信号员维持各部队联络。"),TEXT("At Amiens, Australian, Canadian, British and French formations advance in neighbouring sectors. Guns, tanks and aircraft support the infantry, ammunition parties bring supplies forward, and signallers maintain contact between units."),TEXT("At Amiens, Australian, Canadian, British and French formations fight on neighbouring fronts. Guns, tanks and aircraft open the passage for infantry. Ammunition parties and signallers decide how long the common timetable can keep running.")},
{TEXT("黑日里的接替令"),TEXT("Relief Orders on a Black Day")},
{TEXT("八月八日的报告不断向后传来，成建制的部队被切断，枪位接连沉默。修复的缴获坦克、反坦克枪与后方炮兵被编在一份应急表上，先替后卫接出一条路。"),TEXT("Reports pour back on 8 August: formed units cut off, gun positions silent. Repaired captured tanks, anti-tank rifles and rear batteries are placed on one emergency table to open a road for the rear guard.")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。亚眠与斯卡尔普开场士气增加四，首轮野炮提前二十二秒，迫击炮提前十二秒。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. Amiens and the Scarpe begin with four additional morale; the first field barrage prepares 22 seconds earlier and mortars 12 seconds earlier.")},
{TEXT("明渠边的接合部"),TEXT("The Junction by the Open Cut")},
{TEXT("澳大利亚军团与配属美军在北面的贝利库尔隧道上方作战。本连在里克瓦尔的明渠旁等待相邻部队回报；法军喷火分遣队被接入电话线，工兵正沿纤道寻找可以渡越的缺口。"),TEXT("Australian and attached American troops fight above the Bellicourt tunnel to the north. This company waits by the open cut at Riqueval for reports from neighbouring formations. A French flame detachment joins the telephone circuit while pioneers seek a passage along the towpath.")},
{TEXT("仍能通行的纤道"),TEXT("The Towpath Still Open")},
{TEXT("明渠坡岸被炮火打坏，残存纤道仍承担交通。烟弹与炮兵联络优先配给渡口，后续塞勒河行动继续按此供给。"),TEXT("Shellfire breaks the canal banks, leaving traffic on the surviving towpath. Smoke and battery liaison receive priority at the crossing; the allocation continues into the Selle operation."),TEXT("明渠两侧土坡已被炮火打坏，交通却必须沿着残存纤道继续。后方把烟弹和少量炮兵联络先送到尚能通行的渡口；这份优先令将跟随后卫一直到塞勒河。")},
{TEXT("获得两枚研究点。运河与塞勒河首轮野炮提前十二秒、迫击炮提前八秒、首轮烟幕后再整备缩短十二秒。"),TEXT("Gain two research points. At the canal and Selle, the first field barrage prepares 12 seconds earlier, mortars eight seconds earlier, and the first smoke rearm takes 12 seconds less.")},
{TEXT("河谷里的铁轨"),TEXT("Rails Through the Valley")},
{TEXT("兴登堡防线已被突破，追击沿塞勒河展开。澳大利亚军团正在休整，其他协约国部队继续前进；本连遇到的铁路火力，把一段切口变成了移动的后卫阵地。"),TEXT("The Hindenburg Line has been breached and the pursuit reaches the Selle. The Australian Corps is resting while other Allied formations continue forward. In this company sector, railway fire has turned a cutting into a moving rear-guard position.")},
{TEXT("撤运掩护"),TEXT("Cover the evacuation")},
{TEXT("撤运掩护"),TEXT("Cover the evacuation"),TEXT("最后一班撤运")},
{TEXT("撤运掩护"),TEXT("Cover the evacuation"),TEXT("The Last Evacuation Train")},
{TEXT("车站里仍堆着未装完的物资。铁路炮组留在湿冷河谷掩护撤运，步兵守住轨道两侧，观察员监视敌军接近。"),TEXT("Stores still await loading at the station. The railway gun crew covers evacuation from the cold valley, infantry hold both sides of the track, and observers watch the enemy approaches.")},
{TEXT("车站里仍堆着未装完的物资。铁路炮组留在湿冷河谷掩护撤运，步兵守住轨道两侧，观察员监视敌军接近。"),TEXT("Stores still await loading at the station. The railway gun crew covers evacuation from the cold valley, infantry hold both sides of the track, and observers watch the enemy approaches."),TEXT("车站里还堆着没有装完的物资。铁路炮组留在湿冷的河谷，步兵替它守住近侧接近线；轨道一旦失去观察，车上的枪也只剩噪音。")},
{TEXT("车站里仍堆着未装完的物资。铁路炮组留在湿冷河谷掩护撤运，步兵守住轨道两侧，观察员监视敌军接近。"),TEXT("Stores still await loading at the station. The railway gun crew covers evacuation from the cold valley, infantry hold both sides of the track, and observers watch the enemy approaches."),TEXT("Unloaded stores still fill the station. The railway gun crew remains in the cold valley while infantry protect the nearby approaches. Without observation along the track, the guns aboard are little more than noise.")},
{TEXT("本关出现装甲列车。运河优先令继续生效；中央补给湾可缩短下一轮整备。"),TEXT("An armoured train operates in this sector. Canal supply priority continues; central stores advance the next preparation cycle.")},
{TEXT("城内的居民"),TEXT("Civilians in town")},
{TEXT("城内的居民"),TEXT("Civilians in town"),TEXT("窗户后的灯")},
{TEXT("城内的居民"),TEXT("Civilians in town"),TEXT("Lights Behind the Windows")},
{TEXT("瓦朗谢讷仍有居民。加拿大军向城郊推进，炮兵重新划定禁射区，老兵带领补充班前进。"),TEXT("Civilians remain in Valenciennes. As Canadian troops approach the outskirts, the batteries mark restricted zones and veterans lead the replacement sections forward.")},
{TEXT("瓦朗谢讷仍有居民。加拿大军向城郊推进，炮兵重新划定禁射区，老兵带领补充班前进。"),TEXT("Civilians remain in Valenciennes. As Canadian troops approach the outskirts, the batteries mark restricted zones and veterans lead the replacement sections forward."),TEXT("瓦朗谢讷仍有居民。加拿大军向城边推进，炮兵重新画出不准覆盖的地段；经验丰富的老兵被分给补充班，把最后几步路带稳。")},
{TEXT("瓦朗谢讷仍有居民。加拿大军向城郊推进，炮兵重新划定禁射区，老兵带领补充班前进。"),TEXT("Civilians remain in Valenciennes. As Canadian troops approach the outskirts, the batteries mark restricted zones and veterans lead the replacement sections forward."),TEXT("Civilians remain in Valenciennes. As Canadian troops approach the town, the batteries redraw the areas they must not cover. Experienced soldiers are distributed among replacement sections to steady the last approaches.")},
{TEXT("军车与手推车"),TEXT("Wagons and Handcarts")},
{TEXT("军车与平民手推车挤在城外道路上。后卫缩小炮火覆盖区，老兵带领补充班换防，掩护其余部队撤离。"),TEXT("Army wagons and civilian handcarts crowd the outer road. The rearguard narrows its fire plan while veterans lead replacement sections into position and cover the withdrawal.")},
{TEXT("军车与平民手推车挤在城外道路上。后卫缩小炮火覆盖区，老兵带领补充班换防，掩护其余部队撤离。"),TEXT("Army wagons and civilian handcarts crowd the outer road. The rearguard narrows its fire plan while veterans lead replacement sections into position and cover the withdrawal."),TEXT("城外道路上，军车与平民手推车挤在一起。后卫的火力表缩小了覆盖区，老兵被派到新兵身边；少一次混乱，就可能多带出一队人。")},
{TEXT("军车与平民手推车挤在城外道路上。后卫缩小炮火覆盖区，老兵带领补充班换防，掩护其余部队撤离。"),TEXT("Army wagons and civilian handcarts crowd the outer road. The rearguard narrows its fire plan while veterans lead replacement sections into position and cover the withdrawal."),TEXT("Army wagons and civilian handcarts crowd the outer road. The rear guard narrows its fire plan and puts veterans beside the replacements. One less panic may bring one more section out.")},
{TEXT("获得一枚研究点。最后两关禁用毒气与空中轰炸；开场士气增加四，首轮野炮提前十二秒，首轮烟幕后再整备缩短十二秒。"),TEXT("Gain one research point. Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited in the final two operations. Opening morale rises by four; the first field barrage prepares 12 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm takes 12 seconds less.")},
{TEXT("最后一周的战斗"),TEXT("The final week of fighting")},
{TEXT("最后一周的战斗"),TEXT("The final week of fighting"),TEXT("城墙外的清晨")},
{TEXT("最后一周的战斗"),TEXT("The final week of fighting"),TEXT("Morning Outside the Walls")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队正在勒凯努瓦方向作战，桑布尔攻势仍在继续。城墙里面还有平民，前沿还没有停火；连部把最后一次接替的名字抄进册子。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops fight towards Le Quesnoy while the Sambre offensive continues. Civilians remain inside the walls, and the front has not ceased fire. The company clerk enters the names for one final relief.")},
{TEXT("折回口袋的电报"),TEXT("The Folded Telegram")},
{TEXT("奥匈帝国的停战协定开始生效，南方盟军已经停止作战。西线仍在开火。军官把电报折回口袋，转身点数还能列队的人。"),TEXT("The Austro-Hungarian armistice comes into force and Germany's southern ally stops fighting. The Western Front still fires. The officer folds the telegram into his pocket and turns to count the men who can still form up.")},
{TEXT("城郊火力限制与老兵接替继续生效。中央易手后的反击，是通向最后出口前的障碍。"),TEXT("The civilian-sector fire restrictions and veteran relief remain in force. A counterstroke at the centre blocks the final exit.")},
